                        "review": "Ehhh.....this is somewhere between thumbs up or down. Game isn't terrible, but:\n\n1) The occasional bug is annoying. I clicked on a sign too fast and it locked my controls. Had to restart the game. \n2) The puzzles aren't moon logic, but sometimes seem slightly off. Like, why would anyone think to use a key ring in a paper cutter? \n3) Gameplay is largely just sweeping through whatever map you're on to see if you can pick up any items. Sometimes, the game will refresh the map with new items, which means doing another sweep through the same rooms - kind of a boring way of setting up puzzles. \n4) [spoiler] The whole point of the story is a that a secret lab funded by the military doesn't have better security protocols surrounding its key technology? Anyone goes rogue and can lie their way into the apocalypse? Not impossible, but its a bit sloppy writing. [/spoiler] \n\n\nIt's an okay point-and-click, but the strength of the writing has its ups and downs. And the sound design trying to keep you high strung with violins doesn't really work when there's nothing there and the gameplay is forcing you to quickly scan through rooms button mashing the pickup to grab whatever items you can. I mean, you can't just keep trying to go \"Boo!\" when there isn't anything scary, right? You're turning your horror story into cheap shock thriller.",
